Deep Packet Inspection & Network Traffic Analyzer
A Java-based Deep Packet Inspection (DPI) system for analyzing
network traffic stored in PCAP files. The project parses packet headers,
inspects application-level information such as TLS SNI/HTTP Host,
applies configurable filtering rules, and produces packet-level
ALLOW/DROP decisions.
Note: This project is a PCAP-based analyzer/filter. It does not
act as a live Windows firewall.

🚀 Key Features
- PCAP packet reading and analysis
- Ethernet, IPv4, TCP and UDP packet parsing
- Source/Destination IP inspection
- Source/Destination port inspection
- TLS SNI (Server Name Indication) extraction
- HTTP Host detection
- IP, domain and port based filtering rules
- Application-based rule support
- Multi-threaded packet processing
- Producer-consumer architecture using thread-safe queues
- Load balancing across packet-processing workers
- Connection/flow tracking
- Forwarded and dropped packet statistics
- Filtered output PCAP generation
- Java Swing GUI for packet visualization
